<answer>Setting the determinant equal to zero since it is given yields \[
0 = 1 \cdot
\begin{vmatrix} x & y \\ y & x \end{vmatrix}
- 4 \cdot
\begin{vmatrix} 3 & y \\ 3 & x \end{vmatrix}
+ 9 \cdot
\begin{vmatrix} 3 & x \\ 3 & y \end{vmatrix}
= (x^2 - y^2) - 4(3x - 3y) + 9(3y - 3x).\]We are given that $x$ and $y$ are distinct, so $x^2 - y^2 \neq 0.$ It follows that \[(x - y)(x + y) - 4 \cdot 3(x - y) + 9 \cdot 3(y - x) = 3(x - y)(x + y - 4 + 9(y - x)) = 3(x - y)(-8x + 10y) = 0.\]From this we deduce that either $x = y$ or $-8x + 10y = 0.$ \end answer

